    <a id="1"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 1</h1>
    <div class="statement">Given a rational straight line and an apotome, if the square on the whole is greater than the square on the annex by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with the whole, and the whole is commensurable in length with the rational line set out, let the apotome be called a <i>first apotome.</i></div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX85/">X.85</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX91/">X.91</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX97/">X.97</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX108/">X.108</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    <br>
  
    <a id="2"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 2</h1>
    <div class="statement">But if the annex is commensurable with the rational straight line set out, and the square on the whole is greater than that on the annex by the square on a straight line commensurable with the whole, let the apotome be called a <i>second apotome.</i></div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX86/">X.86</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX92/">X.92</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX98/">X.98</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX109/">X.109</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX111/">X.111</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    <br>
  
    <a id="3"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 3</h1>
    <div class="statement">But if neither is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, and the square on the whole is greater than the square on the annex by the square on a straight line commensurable with the whole, let the apotome be called a <i>third apotome.</i></div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX87/">X.87</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX93/">X.93</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX99/">X.99</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX110/">X.110</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    <br>
  
    <a id="4"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 4</h1>
    <div class="statement">Again, if the square on the whole is greater than the square on the annex by the square on a straight line incommensurable with the whole, then, if the whole is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, let the apotome be called a <i>fourth apotome</i>;</div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX88/">X.88</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX94/">X.94</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX100/">X.100</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX108/">X.108</a></td></tr>
  <tr><th>Book XIII</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookXIII/propositions/propXIII11/">XIII.11</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    <br>
  
    <a id="5"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 5</h1>
    <div class="statement">If the annex be so commensurable, a <i>fifth</i>;</div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX89/">X.89</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX95/">X.95</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX101/">X.101</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX109/">X.109</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    <br>
  
    <a id="6"></a>
    <div class="theorem">
    <h1>Definition 6</h1>
    <div class="statement">And, if neither, a <i>sixth</i>.</div>
    </div>
    
    
<h4>Referenced by</h4>
<table class="ref-table">
  <tr><th>Book X</th><td><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX90/">X.90</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX96/">X.96</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX102/">X.102</a>, <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX110/">X.110</a></td></tr>
  
</table>
    
  
  





